<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    arcfox overlay of Launcher3's device_profiles.xml.

    THE ONLY CHANGE IS THAT THE 3_by_3 grid-option IS DELETED. Everything else is
    a verbatim copy of upstream; diff against
    packages/apps/Launcher3/res/xml/device_profiles.xml before touching it.

    WHY. Launcher3 picks a grid by EUCLIDEAN DISTANCE, not by thresholds
    (InvariantDeviceProfile.java:916-918), from the MINIMUM availableSize across
    every supported bound of EVERY display, and it TRANSPOSES landscape entries
    (:902-905). On a flip mixing a 1080x2640 inner panel with a 1080x1272 cover,
    the two minima come from different panels:

        minWidthPx  = 943  (inner panel, LANDSCAPE, transposed)
        minHeightPx = 849  (cover panel, PORTRAIT, insets 74+349 removed)
        at density 420 gives 359.24 x 323.43 dp

    That geometry belongs to no physical panel, and the nearest option to it was
    3_by_3 (255,300) at distance 106.84, the smallest grid Launcher3 ships,
    beating 4_by_5 (275,420) at 128.15. Measured consequence: a 3x3 home screen on
    a 1080x2640 panel, a 3 slot hotseat, and default_workspace_4x5.xml never read
    (each grid-option names its own defaultLayoutId, and default_workspace_3x3.xml
    contains no appwidget element at all, which is why no widgets appeared).

    With 3_by_3 removed the nearest becomes 4_by_5 at 128.15.

    DO NOT "fix" this by lowering 4_by_5's minHeightDps instead. That was the first
    proposal and it does NOT work: against 3_by_3's 106.84, 4_by_5 scores 121.51 at
    minHeightDps 411, 113.84 at 400, 107.37 at 390, all still losing, and only wins
    below about 389, by 0.09. Far too thin to ship.

    This is a device-local workaround, not the real fix. The real fix is to stop
    aggregating across display profiles and derive the grid from the ACTIVE
    display; that belongs upstream and would retire this file. A third route is
    making getDeviceType() report TYPE_MULTI_DISPLAY, which filters 3_by_3 out by
    deviceCategory (it is phone only) with no distance tuning at all.
-->
